I left out the `http-client` enrichment. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, and a graph-definition change that hasn't been made yet can't widen that grant. The enrichment would also send each item's untrusted text to an external host, and it wouldn't affect the output. The body below implements `DropSeen` with the state-read grant only.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

